  KEY ENGINEERING TAKEAWAYS (docs/BENCHMARKS.md:250):
  1. RAW SPEED: NPU wins by 0.92x over DirectML FP16 (6.6ms vs 6.1ms).
  2. ACCURACY:  DirectML FP16 retains full FP32 accuracy (+4.53 mAP@50-95 over AdaRound INT8).
  3. TRADEOFF:  DirectML requires 0 quantization effort (one-line convert, no calibration/head-cut).
                NPU is worth it when the last 30-40% of latency is critical; otherwise iGPU FP16 is optimal.

